From 960bb633c5538d4eb635169e9cd1c56e89834303 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:20:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/59] M3: BBSC billboards turn their bones to the camera

Ported from WhiteoutFlakes io/m3/m3_billboard.cpp (CBBSolver::ApplyBillboard):
types 0 to 6, look-at or view direction, the correction quaternions, the
spin of root-level bones, and the division back through the parent so the
subtree follows. Run per skeleton update in world space, as the game does.
BBSC is parsed (billboardbehavior.ts); SC2 sets no BONE billboard flags.

Known defects: at rest (sequence -1) the skin uses no bone matrices, so
billboards show only while a sequence plays; type 4 is not applied, as in
the game.
